  << java.util.HexFormat as an immutable value: case, delimiter, prefix and
     suffix, each with-method returning a new HexFormat. Output Strings are
     plain SLeeLa Strings built by concatenation. The long, int, short, byte
     and char forms of toHexDigits(value) cannot be told apart by the VM, so
     only toHexDigits(value, digits) is implemented; the one-argument form
     throws and says why.  The
     parse side reads its text as UTF-16 code units (through javaStringFromUtf8)
     and follows the JDK algorithm: no-delimiter strings must have an even
     length, delimited strings must match the prefix, digits, suffix and
     delimiter stride exactly, and digit values wrap to 32 or 64 bits as Java
     does. Error messages quote the offending text for ASCII characters (via
     JavaText). The Appendable forms of formatHex and hashCode keep their
